Recommends: dmg2img
Description: Get Wi-Fi and Bluetooth firmware from macOS (T2 Macs)
 get-apple-firmware retrieves the Broadcom Wi-Fi/Bluetooth firmware blobs
 that Apple T2 Macs require from a macOS installation, an Apple recovery
 image, or a previously prepared EFI partition, and installs them under
 /lib/firmware/brcm/.
 .
 This is the upstream t2linux "firmware.sh" helper, packaged for Debian.
 The pristine upstream source is shipped as documentation
 (upstream/firmware.sh) and the installed helper is a minimal, reviewed
 patch that pins the runtime-downloaded helper code to an immutable commit
 and verifies its SHA-256 before execution. The helper is a Bash script
 that embeds a Python 3 archive-renamer using only the standard library.
 .
 The optional "download from Apple's CDN" path (get_from_online)
 additionally requires curl and dmg2img, and downloads a macOS Recovery
 Image at run time; that path is not required for the EFI or macOS-host
 retrieval modes.
